1. Project licence

   The source code is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The full
   text is in LICENSE-APACHE-2.0. This covers everything that is executed or
   compiled: the simulation engine, the benchmark runner, the scenario DSL
   and scripts, the task generators, the web interfaces, the tools and the
   tests, together with the configuration and the city profile that drive
   them.

     https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

   The generated data is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
   International licence (CC BY 4.0). The full text is in LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0.
   This covers:

     - kierston/sim_data/ and the published sim_data archives, except the
       files listed in section 2
     - KDAY day exports (.bin), KSTATE checkpoints and KDIF scenario diffs
     - benchmark tasks, runs and scores
     - the documentation and the paper

     https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

   Attribution under either licence is satisfied by keeping this copyright
   notice and naming the project. The citation in CITATION.cff is the
   preferred form.

   Sections 2 and 3 name the third-party inputs that carry their own terms.
   Those terms take precedence for the files they list.


2. Data redistributed under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0

   The files below contain, or are adapted from, a substantial part of the
   OpenStreetMap database, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors. They are a
   Derivative Database under ODbL 1.0 and are made available under ODbL 1.0,
   not under CC BY 4.0.

     https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
     https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

   Raw extracts, in kierston/init-inputs.tar.zst under sources/<city>/:

     buildings_geom.json     Overpass building export
     pois_export.json        Overpass point-of-interest export
     topology.graphml        road network, downloaded with OSMnx
     geocode_cache.json      Nominatim reverse-geocoding results

   Files derived from them, in kierston/sim_data/ and in the published
   sim_data archives:

     buildings.json          building footprints, kinds, levels, addresses
     dwellings.json          the dwelling stock, per OSM building
     pois.json               the point-of-interest catalogue
     car_graph.bin           the drivable road graph
     workplaces.json         worksites, by OSM name and coordinate
     schools.json            schools, by OSM name and coordinate
     orgs.json               organisations with premises, by OSM name and
                             coordinate

   If you redistribute any of these files, or a database adapted from them,
   you must keep the OpenStreetMap attribution and offer it under ODbL 1.0.


3. Data redistributed under other third-party terms

   kierston/init-inputs.tar.zst, sources/<city>/opencellid_local.json
     Adapted from the OpenCelliD database, (c) Unwired Labs. Creative Commons
     Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International.
     https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

   kierston/reference/tac_table.json
     Cut from MoazEb/tac-database. MIT licence; the copyright and permission
     notice are at https://github.com/MoazEb/tac-database

   The remaining third-party inputs are United States government works in the
   public domain, or public records. ATTRIBUTION.md lists every source, what it
   is used for and where it enters the pipeline.


4. What sections 2 and 3 do not cover

   Everything else falls under section 1 alone, as Apache 2.0 or CC BY 4.0. In particular, none of the
   following is a Derivative Database of OpenStreetMap, and none of it is
   offered under ODbL or CC BY-SA:

     - the source code, which reads the data above and does not contain it
     - the rest of kierston/sim_data/: population, identity, kinship, ties,
       dockets, vehicles, holdings, accounts, devices, banking, towers and the
       other generated records
     - KDAY day exports (.bin), KSTATE checkpoints and KDIF scenario diffs
     - benchmark tasks, runs, scores and the paper

   Works produced using OpenStreetMap data still carry the attribution:
   "Contains information from OpenStreetMap, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors,
   made available under the Open Database License."
